From 509681277dd93480107d19bd75e925f60b5ddedf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:35:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: opaque 3D in one pass (no-discard program where no
 texel is transparent), uncapped decoding after loading screens, 720x408 by
 default

- Batched opaque faces: one pass at the true depth with depth writes (THPS_R3D_PREPASS=1: the
  depth pass then colour of t20-t23). Faces whose texels (8x8 cells of the cache slot, over the
  span GlVert.uvr gives) hold no transparent one, and untextured faces, go through a program
  with no discard, drawn without blending and with alpha (the mask bit) kept: with discard in a
  program the GPU shades every pixel of every face. The program is gl_draw_fast_fs without its
  three discards, compiled last; rejected, those faces keep the fast program
  (THPS_GL_NODISCARD=0: not built). [gl] line: opaque batched tris without / with discard.
- Texture decoding: the first 8 decodes a frame were outside the THPS_GL_DECODEMS budget, and at
  a level's start each took ~7 ms (56 ms frames, with the GPU on the per-pixel lookup of the pages
  not yet decoded: swap ~260 ms). Now 2 are free. The 30 frames after a stretch of 30 without 3D
  (loading screens, menus) decode every page they draw (THPS_GL_WARMFRAMES=n, 0 off), logged
  with the pages and time it took.
- 720x408 by default (t23: GPU ~50 ms a frame at 960x544, ~25 at 720x408); THPS_VITA_RES=960x544
  for the full resolution. Smoothing stays on (a filtered present, not the cost).
- The program cache logs why a saved program wasn't taken or saved (t23 compiled all 4 at
  every start).
